<BaseLayout title="JuggleCast: a different approach to self-hosted radio automation" description="Compare JuggleCast’s dedicated playout architecture with script-centric self-hosted radio automation approaches, without product-ranking claims."><section class="page container"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">ARCHITECTURAL CHOICE</p><h1>An alternative approach to AzuraCast-style radio automation</h1><p>JuggleCast and AzuraCast are distinct projects. JuggleCast takes a purpose-built scheduling and playout approach; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by AzuraCast.</p></header><div class="prose"><h2>Compare approaches, not scorecards</h2><p>JuggleCast connects its control plane to a dedicated Rust playout engine through explicit station configuration. It does not put a JuggleCast-generated Liquidsoap scripting layer between the scheduler and runtime.</p><p>This can reduce the number of layers an operator inspects. The trade-off is equally important: mature, script-centric ecosystems may offer broader integrations, community knowledge and general-purpose customization. Evaluate those needs against JuggleCast’s focused model.</p><h2>Programming and transitions</h2><p>JuggleCast can incorporate BPM into playlist selection and exposes fade, overlap, bridge, exit, queue and prefetch controls. Optional Pro functionality may add documented Bliss acoustic-similarity strategies. These signals supplement operator programming; they do not guarantee a particular sound.</p><h2>Preview maturity</h2><p>JuggleCast is a Preview, not a production-grade claim. Public images may not exist for every tag and architecture. Endurance, rollback, rootless Docker, large-library performance and disaster-recovery qualification are incomplete.</p><p>Review the <a href="https://github.com/chourmovs/JuggleCast-Community/blob/main/docs/community/known-limitations.md">current limitations</a>, then see the <a href={withBase('installation')}>installation requirements</a> or <a href={withBase('liquidsoap-alternative')}>deeper architecture explanation</a>.</p><aside class="notice">AzuraCast and Liquidsoap are independent projects and may be protected names or marks. No affiliation, sponsorship or endorsement is implied.</aside></div></section><CallToAction/></BaseLayout>
